    "input": "search_document: Good morning,\n\nThank you for reaching out to Northwind Outdoor support. I understand your concern regarding the deduction of points from your loyalty account.\n\nBased on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the information regarding point expiration and deductions:\n\n1.  **Point Expiration:** Loyalty points are valid for 12 months from the date they were earned. For example, points earned on January 15, 2024, expire on January 14, 2025. The handbook states that expiration dates are not extended for points that have already been earned [loyalty_program.3].\n2.  **Deductions for Returns:** Points are also deducted if an order is subsequently returned or cancelled. If your balance drops below zero due to returns, you must make a new purchase to restore your standing before redeeming rewards [loyalty_program.2].\n3.  **Earning Rate:** You earn 1 loyalty point for every $1.00 spent on eligible items [loyalty_program.2].\n\nThe handbook excerpts do not contain specific details on how to review individual account history, investigate specific calculation errors, or manually adjust point balances. Therefore, I cannot verify if there was an error in your specific expiration calculation or if the deduction was due to a return/cancellation.\n\nI recommend checking your account dashboard to see your current balance and the expiration dates of your oldest points, as this is the recommended method to monitor your rewards [loyalty_program.3].\n\nSince the handbook does not cover the process for disputing specific account discrepancies or investigating potential errors in point calculations, I must offer to escalate this ticket to a human agent who can review your specific account history and transaction details.\n\nWould you like me to escalate this to a human agent for further investigation?",
